course: dictionary
lesson: 8300
title: Riverside words and describing words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The riverside is the land along or near a river. In «Wolves were wiped out from Yellowstone by the 1920s», we learn about wildlife, but the word we need is riverside. In «the riverside trees grew back», riverside tells you where the trees were: next to the river.
explain: Riverside can also describe things. Put it before a noun and it tells you what kind of thing it is: a riverside walk, a riverside path, a riverside café. Here riverside is an adjective, so it describes the noun after it.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «They sculled home to their own cosy riverside parlour» tells you the parlour is near the river, and the words around it show it is a home, not a shop. Ask yourself: where is it, or what kind of thing is it?
explain: Towns often grew up by the riverside, because rivers gave water, food and a way to travel. So when you see riverside on a map or in a story, think about the river and the people who lived there.
fact: The riverside is the land along or near a river.
fact: Riverside before a noun describes something next to a river, such as a riverside walk or a riverside café.
fact: When riverside comes before a noun, it is an adjective, because it describes the noun.
fact: Many towns grew up by the riverside because rivers gave water, food and transport.
fact: «In Yellowstone Park, returning wolves reduced the number of deer and the riverside trees grew back.» Here riverside tells us where the trees grew.
exercise: «They wandered along the riverside, watching the boats.» Where did they wander? | *Along the bank of the river | Inside a museum | In a shop
exercise: «We cycled on the riverside path.» Which word means next to a river? | path | cycled | *riverside
exercise: «Elk changed where they grazed, letting some riverside trees grow again.» What does riverside describe here? | *The trees, which grew beside the river | The wolves | Grazing | The elk
test: «The riverside park was full of families on a sunny Sunday.» What is riverside describing? | A boat race | A busy road | A kind of sandwich | *A park beside a river
test: Which word means land along a river? | Woodland | *Riverside | Cliff | Hilltop
exam: In «a riverside café», what job does riverside do? | It names a place, the riverside | It means busy | *It describes the café, so it is an adjective | It is a verb for sitting
